atchRatio":0.47450000000000003},{"ratio":0.88,"watchRatio":0.4693},{"ratio":0.89,"watchRatio":0.4661},{"ratio":0.9,"watchRatio":0.4646},{"ratio":0.91,"watchRatio":0.4585},{"ratio":0.92,"watchRatio":0.4531},{"ratio":0.93,"watchRatio":0.449},{"ratio":0.94,"watchRatio":0.4459},{"ratio":0.95,"watchRatio":0.44049999999999995},{"ratio":0.96,"watchRatio":0.4325},{"ratio":0.97,"watchRatio":0.4233},{"ratio":0.98,"watchRatio":0.41100000000000003},{"ratio":0.99,"watchRatio":0.3969},{"ratio":1,"watchRatio":0.3918}],"script":{"source_path":"all-146-tagged.json","words":158,"wpm":null,"lang":"en","chapters":[],"blocks":[],"text":"In the 1970s, Guyanese Hindus went to jail for cooking a roti. The CIA put the man who banned it in power. Here's what happened. Cheddi Jagan led British Guiana into independence in 1960s. He was Indo-Guyanese. The Americans called him a communist. They decided he had to go. The CIA backed Forbes Burnham, Jagan's old friend and a current rival. Burnham's party joined with European right-wing faction. The 1964 election was rigged. Jagan lost. Once in power, Burnham turned on Indians who had supported Jagan. He went after what they ate. &gt;&gt; And in the uh '60s and the '70s, there was policies that limited the rice and potatoes and all of these things that are Indian staples. &gt;&gt; Roti became a contraband food. Police raided wedding houses and Ramayana readings. People went to jail. Administration found many ways to oppress Hindus. The files were declassified in 2020. Kennedy himself approved the operation. Follow for more stories."}}